  partName: Exhaust Manifold Left
  description: The Exhaust Manifold Left is a large, elongated metal component located
    at the middle-left-center of the engine, responsible for collecting and directing
    exhaust gases from the cylinders to the exhaust system. Its metal-bright material
    helps to withstand high temperatures, and its position allows for efficient exhaust
    gas flow. Interestingly, the Exhaust Manifold Left is designed to work in tandem
    with its right counterpart to maintain engine balance.
